# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GW Immobilier — example environment configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public display settings use NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# Admin credentials and session secrets are server-only: never use NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Set the private admin variables in Vercel Project Settings before unpausing.
# Empty admin variables intentionally keep login disabled (fail closed).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# WhatsApp Business line — digits only, international format, no "+" or spaces.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=213600000000

# Phone number shown in the header, footer and contact page.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PHONE_NUMBER=+213 00 00 00 00

# Public contact e-mail.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_EMAIL=contact@gw-immobilier.example

# Canonical base URL, used by the sitemap and OpenGraph metadata.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://gw-immobilier.vercel.app

# Public customer catalog mode:
# - Empty: demo data in development; database-backed catalog in production.
# - "demo": explicitly opt into the prototype seed data (internal previews only).
# Never set "demo" on a public/customer-facing production deployment.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CATALOG_MODE=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL persistence (use the pooled HTTPS/connection string from the provider)
# DATABASE_URL is server-only. Do not expose it with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# Apply db/migrations/0001_initial.sql before enabling admin record operations.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Protected admin access — configure these as private server environment vars.
# ADMIN_EMAIL: the administrator e-mail address.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD: a unique password with at least 16 characters.
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET: a random secret, at least 32 characters.
# Generate a session secret locally with:
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
# Do not commit real values or expose them to the browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ADMIN_EMAIL=
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=
